qmd 2.5.3: read a natural-language lex query as an OR of its content words

A lex query is parsed as keywords: every word, ANDed, each as a prefix
("w"*). A question ("how is the storage ring RF frequency tuned") then
asks for a document holding all of its words, function words included,
and the prefixes of "a", "the", "is" match nearly every row, so the
query is both slow and usually empty. A query that contains a stopword
or ends with "?", and uses no explicit syntax (quotes, -negation), is
now read as a question: its non-stopword terms are ORed without prefix
expansion and bm25 ranks the matches. Keyword queries and explicit
syntax keep the existing parse.

Applies to the published package (dist/) with `patch -p1` from the
package root, after 0001 and 0002.

